Z||000000||85ZainoGT||08-10-2001||06:00 PM||||I have heard the sunroof comes out?  can someone tell me how to do it please? thanks||||reg||5
Z||000001||JBGehling||08-10-2001||06:24 PM||||mmmm... a quick explanation:<BR>1)unlatch the sunroof.<BR>2)Press the two buttons on the sides of the black piece together and then you will be able to pull the sunroof out of the black piece.<BR>3)get outside and push the sunroof up from the inside so you can get a grip on it and then wiggle it out of the two holes in the front part of the sunroof.<BR>4) store it in the front trunk<P>...<BR>If that doesn't help... oh well, it's really a simple process, you just have to play around with it.<BR>Josh||||reg||1
Z||000002||b lo 0||08-10-2001||07:18 PM||||I had a removable sunroof before, so it was elementary for me, but JB is right. Just DO NOT drop it or hit it on anything.  There is not a frame around the glass like my old Nissan.  Also, when putting it back in make sure the tabs go into both slots (the tabs rotate) and all the way in or it will not close all the way.  Enjoy, fellow '85 GT-er!<P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="1">'85 GT (in progress)<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">       <BR>White Lightnin!  (NOT moonshine, for all you hillbillies!)</FONT><BR><A HREF="http://www.audioimagery.vstoreauto.com.com" TARGET=_blank>Audio Imagery</A>, budget-priced car audio supplies from people like Monster Cable, Sony & more!||||reg||1
